					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/snorlison" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(222125); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=222125&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610140247" alt="snorlison" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=222125)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/snorlison" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(222125); return false;" >snorlison</a></span> <span class="odate time_1224262376 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Oct 2008 16:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-285668">
									

<p>It is advised that <a href="/scp-124">SCP-124</a> NOT be brought in the vicinity of SCP-073 until such time is determined that SCP-124 should be neutralized. It is unknown if SCP-073's flora destruction field would destroy SCP-124's fecund effects, but in any case let's not risk losing a valuable Foundation asset.</p>
<p>Proposal: SCP-073 posses a destructive field detrimental to plant material as well as the flora supporting qualities of soil. SCP-124 is a sample of soil that posses qualities that can greatly enhance life, including plant life. This proposal suggests testing SCP-073 flora destruction field against the results of plants grown in SCP-124.</p>

							</div>

								
