					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rigen" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2826105); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2826105&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610140247" alt="Rigen" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2826105)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rigen" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2826105); return false;" >Rigen</a></span> <span class="odate time_1525808600 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 May 2018 19:43</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3794342">
									

<p>Mushrooms are not plants. For starter plants, as in <em>Plantae</em> kingdom classification, generally have to produce their own food through photosynthesis. Mushroom, as in organism in <em>Fungi</em> kingdom classification strictly obtains food from somewhere else, sometimes through plant symbiote such as in Lichen, or through fermenting organic materials such as in Natto and moldy bread.</p>
<p>Furthermore, plant cell walls are made of cellulose, compared to most fungi that have chitinous cell walls. The structure of mycellium found in fungal fruit bodies is also fairly different compared to structure of plant matters. Fungal reproduction generally doesn't have sexual system i.e. only one kind of cell exist that could merge with other cell to produce new individual, instead of two kind found in generative stage of most plants.</p>
<p><a href="https://study.com/academy/lesson/the-evolution-of-plants-and-fungi-characteristics-evolutionary-history.html">https://study.com/academy/lesson/the-evolution-of-plants-and-fungi-characteristics-evolutionary-history.html</a></p>

