					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/noaqiyeum" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(191421); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=191421&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610140247" alt="Noaqiyeum" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=191421)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/noaqiyeum" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(191421); return false;" >Noaqiyeum</a></span> <span class="odate time_1227325249 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Nov 2008 03:40</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-315422">
									

<p>Another question about the nature of Cain's immunity to damage. Is this simply a matter of the biological effects of the attack being conferred to the attacker? Or is whatever energy caused the effects (kinetic and thermal being the most likely, I think) redirected onto the attacker?</p>
<p>Take an actual combat situation, for example. Suppose someone were to kick Cain in the stomach. Any normal person would be pushed backwards by the kick, in addition to receiving bruises to the same area. Would the attacker be himself pushed backwards and bruised, or simply bruised (and Cain is forced backwards)? If it is the former, some very interesting Portal-like effects could result from strategic attacks.</p>
<p>However, my current understanding of the report is that all energy that results in negative anatomical consequences is redirected into the attacker and all other energy is retained by Cain.</p>
<hr />
<p>Second question. Suppose Cain is in an environment would be causing injury to a non-SCP but there is no animate person or object for the damage to be transferred to - an area of crushing gravity, for instance, or a lava flow. Would Cain be injured for having placed himself in such a situation? Or would the damaging energy simply disappear somewhere?</p>

