				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-voss" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(289730); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=289730&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610140247" alt="Dr Voss" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=289730)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-voss" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(289730); return false;" >Dr Voss</a></span> <span class="odate time_1236891130 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">12 Mar 2009 20:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-413494">
									

<p>He's got a point though. There's no mention of 073 having any kind of telekinetic ability, and while any ordinary human can turn a page by blowing on it, doing so is a bit difficult. Flicking through an 800 page book in a minute and a half in a manner that makes every page fully visible for even the briefest of instants is no mean feat (that's nearly nine pages per second). Now try doing that without being allowed to touch the book. Certainly not something that is impossible by the standards we're used to at the Foundation, but not something that anything in 073's description indicates it to be capable of.</p>
<p>Mind you, fixing this should be trivial. Make the book out of something else than plant matter. Maybe plastic is far enough removed from its origin to be unaffected. Or it could be parchment, which 073 should be able to handle without any problem. Or maybe he didn't read a book, but instead watched the information flash by on a screen.</p>

							</div>

								
